    "closure": "every Shape-A split biform has separation rank at least ceil((e+1)/3)",
    "statement": "On Shape A, d_A=1 partitions U_0 into the three source-root classes M_alpha,M_beta,M_theta. The first-degree marked-source frame gives sr(Qbar)=e+1 for the same primitive locator used by the quadratic branch. The dual-MDS identity H_x=omega_x Qbar(t,x)/Lambda_A=G(t,x)/L_U0'(x), with omega_x proportional to ell_gamma on M_gamma, shows that every evaluated locator row lies in one of three fixed quadratic multiples of the span of the evaluated G rows. Evaluation on U_0 preserves both ranks because |U_0| exceeds both X-degree bounds. Hence e+1<=3sr(G), so officially sr(G)>=ceil((e+1)/3)=61083979322.",
